Build the dedicated profile editor required by decision D1 (`design/project-channel.md` §7.2). The current editor is `client/src/components/team-view/TeamMemberDrawer.vue`, a `max-w-[32rem]` side panel with tabs about/persona/knowledge/tools — it cannot host a voice catalog, an audition player and a persona prompt at once.

1. New route `/profiles/:name/edit` + `client/src/views/profile-editor/ProfileEditorView.vue`:
   - single column with a sticky bottom save bar on mobile, two columns (section nav + content) at `lg` and up;
   - sections: About, Persona (reuse `Document` for view mode and `ContentEditorModal.vue` for "edit with chat"), **Voice** (new), Knowledge (reuse `components/profiles/ProfileKnowledgeEditor.vue`), Tools (reuse `ToolDetailsModal.vue` patterns), Model/API, Autonomy.
   - Reuse the existing draft/submit logic patterns from `TeamMemberDrawer.vue` and the profile service already used by `TeamView.vue` — do not fork a second profile API client.
   - Mobile-first: usable at 360 px, no horizontal scroll, all actions ≥44 px.

2. `client/src/views/profile-editor/VoiceSection.vue`:
   - first show the RESOLVED voice preview: "This profile will sound like **Kokoro af_bella** — inherited from project" (uses `GET /api/profiles/{name}/voice`);
   - then an optional override: voice picker grouped by locality/language from `GET /api/media/voices`, a play button per voice calling `POST /api/media/voices/preview` with a sample sentence, a speed slider, a style field and a language field;
   - when the preview endpoint answers 503, the play buttons are disabled with the provider's reason shown inline (no fake success, no spinner forever);
   - an `enabled` toggle meaning "this profile speaks / stays silent" with an explicit hint of what silence does to a video;
   - re-validate the `PUT /api/profiles/{name}/voice` payload stays small (no sample bytes in the profile file).

3. `TeamMemberDrawer.vue` gains an "Open full editor" link (router push) in its header or per tab; every existing drawer behaviour keeps working unchanged. Do not reformat that file.

4. If the profile editor is reachable from `TeamView.vue`, add the entry point there too; keep the diff minimal.

Acceptance: client builds (report the exact command used); the editor loads a real profile, edits its voice, saves and reloads showing the new resolved voice; with `voice` absent the UI shows the inherited resolution and saves without adding noise; drawer and team view still work.
